    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18271" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφήκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>arrive at or have arrived,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἷ πάντα δεῖ ἀφήκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					530e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς θεούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					52.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς πρῖσιν ἀ.</span>
			<i>is a case</i> for operation, <i><span class="en">
